				\begin{document}$$Y= {\beta }_{0}+ {\beta }_{1}{X}_{1}+{\beta }_{2}{X}_{2}+{\beta }_{3}{X}_{3}+{\beta }_{4}{X}_{4}+{\beta }_{5}{X}_{5}+{\beta }_{11}{X}_{1}^{2}+{\beta }_{22}{X}_{2}^{2}+{\beta }_{33}{X}_{3}^{2}+{\beta }_{44}{X}_{4}^{2}+{\beta }_{55}{X}_{5}^{2}+ {\beta }_{12}{X}_{1}{X}_{2}+ {\beta }_{13}{X}_{1}{X}_{3}+ {\beta }_{15}{X}_{1}{X}_{5}+ {\beta }_{23}{X}_{2}{X}_{3}+ {\beta }_{24}{X}_{2}{X}_{4}+ {\beta }_{25}{X}_{2}{X}_{5}+ {\beta }_{34}{X}_{3}{X}_{4}+ {\beta }_{35}{X}_{3}{X}_{5}+ {\beta }_{45}{X}_{4}{X}_{5}$$\end{document}Y=β0+β1X1+β2X2+β3X3+β4X4+β5X5+β11X12+β22X22+β33X32+β44X42+β55X52+β12X1X2+β13X1X3+β15X1X5+β23X2X3+β24X2X4+β25X2X5+β34X3X4+β35X3X5+β45X4X5where Y is the response, β0 is the intercept, and X1–X5 are the coded levels of the five growth parameters. The model includes β₁–β₅ as linear coefficients, β₁₁–β₅₅ as quadratic terms, and β₁₂, β₁₃, β₁₅, β₂₃, β₂₄, β₂₅, β₃₄, β₃₅, and β₄₅ capturing interactions among these factors. For culture conditions that significantly fit the model, we evaluated model adequacy and parameter effects using ANOVA, Pareto charts, contour plots, and desirability plots.

The seven C. tropicalis isolates were assessed under the experimental conditions summarized in Table S3. Optimization of growth conditions for C. tropicalis biofilm formation was initially screened using CV assay. Among the tested cultures (six clinical isolates and one standard reference strain), four clinical isolates—C4, U873, U951, and U1179—exhibited responses that were statistically compatible with the CCD model when grown on polypropylene surfaces. The CCD analysis evaluated both linear (L) and quadratic (Q) contributions of the experimental variables to biofilm formation. For the C4 isolate, the interaction between temperature (1L) and pH (2Q) emerged as the principal determinant. In the U873 strain, significant effects were observed for temperature–pH (1L × 2L) and temperature–incubation time (1L × 5L) interactions. The U951 isolate showed a strong interaction between temperature and incubation period (1L × 5L), whereas for U1179, temperature and pH (1L × 2L) formed the key interacting pair. These four isolates exceeded the standardized effect threshold (p = 0.05) on the Pareto chart (Fig. 1), while the remaining strains did not meet significance criteria (Fig. S3). Contour and desirability plots (Figs. 2 and 3) revealed the stationary points of the response surfaces, enabling identification of the most influential parameter combinations. ANOVA confirmed meaningful factor contributions for isolates C4, U873, U951, and U1179 based on their respective F-statistics and significance levels (Tables S4, S5, S6, and S7). Corresponding second-order regression equations generated from the CCD-RSM analysis are presented in Eqs. 2–5.2\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
